census-batch39.log — span eight, the leaf basepoints

Program: census-batch39.c (cc -O2 -o census39 census-batch39.c)
Model: leaf conditions HighAt (p-3) 8 and LowAt 0 (p+3) on the arm, the full crookedness
clause family Cl(a,b)/Dl(a,b) for all 0 <= a, a+3 <= b <= 8, one dichotomy split, and
three-leg walk shapes of length at most 18.  Positive answers are sound (the automaton
over-approximates the class of arms); negative answers are relative to the model.

$ ./census39 8 18 1 3
######## span 8, basepoint 3 ########
  SPLIT at (0,7):
    LowAt  branch: [2,3,4,5,6,5,4,3,2,1,2,3,4,5,6,7]
    HighAt branch: [2,3,4,5,4,3,2,1,2,3,4,5,6,7]

$ ./census39 8 18 1 5
######## span 8, basepoint 5 ########
  SPLIT at (1,8):
    LowAt  branch: [6,5,4,3,4,5,6,7,6,5,4,3,2,1,0]
    HighAt branch: [6,5,4,3,2,3,4,5,6,7,6,5,4,3,2,1,0]

$ ./census39 8 18 1 4
######## span 8, basepoint 4 ########
  NOT SOLVED at depth 1, maxlen 18

The four walks of the two solved basepoints are exactly the ones formalised in
HPC/Fold/Span8.lean (basepoint 5 uses the reflected walk, one time shorter: the search's
trailing 0 is not needed).
